{"condition_compatibility":"compatible","confidence":0.82,"content_digest":"7b6792ba1b5c4e512f8715f977292ac272dcd260583e63e10cd97dd79900549d","created_at":"2026-08-22T19:32:01+00:00","direction":"principle_to_meta","generation_trace":[{"attempts":1,"input_sha256":"0b0582c2b5c2718f87e084e05d53915f96ed0c241966cc54db1af1af228d8a7b","input_tokens":5580,"latency_ms":24763,"model":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Flash","output_sha256":"c48c14376f3346121fd298a26f0a0b5c06b94260def5030887c3e6602dad4f92","output_tokens":2717,"prompt_sha256":"a0e24249a3438877119c33b7ce1b688152e1189df5765ebd53fae91f7c321069","prompt_template":"meta-grounding-v1","provider":"siliconflow","repair_attempted":false,"schema_valid":true,"transport_attempts":1}],"link_id":"foundation-link:7a6e306685d300788de0b4dc","meta_principle_id":"meta:neuroscience-cognition:sparse-coding","meta_principle_revision":1,"principle_id":"prn:neuroscience-cognition:01M0NFA244Y6WZH90DZ79HMA9G","principle_revision":1,"rationale":"The sparse-coding meta-principle establishes that sparse generative models of natural images can yield localized, edge-like receptive fields. The new principle refines this by showing that the parameterization of the prior is a decisive control variable for those outcomes, so the meta-principle's applicability depends on proper prior tuning.","relation_type":"refines","review_attestation":{"actor":"principia-owner","basis":"Explicit Submit reviewed changeset confirmation in local Admin","reviewed_at":"2026-08-23T02:58:57+00:00","source_review_status":"unassessed","trace_id":"sync:01M0P5WC937PV7PKQMASBZ4D3Z"},"review_status":"reviewed","revision":1,"scale_compatibility":"partial","schema_version":"global-foundation-link-v1","status":"active","updated_at":"2026-08-22T19:32:01+00:00","variable_compatibility":"compatible"}
{"condition_compatibility":"compatible","confidence":0.62,"content_digest":"b527be611c9119c59fb025b9585ad9fde946984ff9eefcaa69d04f7bfaf34a8b","created_at":"2026-08-23T13:20:27+00:00","direction":"meta_to_principle","generation_trace":[{"attempts":1,"input_sha256":"1e2c32f0bda735d7e4c6e63398f61689e11927d755fa676b98a2682f59666b8c","input_tokens":6069,"latency_ms":35655,"model":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Flash","output_sha256":"062c2874b1c4746dd9a9c91f043b86a81aca41694b285c9272ffc176ba982431","output_tokens":2405,"prompt_sha256":"a0e24249a3438877119c33b7ce1b688152e1189df5765ebd53fae91f7c321069","prompt_template":"meta-grounding-v1","provider":"siliconflow","repair_attempted":false,"schema_valid":true,"transport_attempts":1}],"link_id":"foundation-link:83097ca19241f0d80b327388","meta_principle_id":"meta:socio-technical-systems:collective-intelligence-process-loss","meta_principle_revision":1,"principle_id":"prn:ai-ml:01M0QCE37F62Y5M82F1ZV3E6V7","principle_revision":1,"rationale":"The meta-principle states that actual group productivity equals potential resources minus process losses such as coordination, communication, and motivation losses. The new principle's non-linear group-size pattern is consistent with this general account: adding members can add resources but also process losses, so quality need not increase linearly with group size. The meta-principle does not predict the exact ordering of sizes 3, 5, and 7, but it provides a compatible general mechanism for the observed non-monotonicity.","relation_type":"consistent_with","review_attestation":{"actor":"principia-owner","basis":"Explicit Submit reviewed changeset confirmation in local Admin","reviewed_at":"2026-08-23T15:24:41+00:00","source_review_status":"unassessed","trace_id":"sync:01M0QKJMJD3A13DCG7YJ3ACW1G"},"review_status":"reviewed","revision":1,"scale_compatibility":"compatible","schema_version":"global-foundation-link-v1","status":"active","updated_at":"2026-08-23T13:20:27+00:00","variable_compatibility":"compatible"}
{"condition_compatibility":"partial","confidence":0.4,"content_digest":"3f2ed6a5816894eb5761f11707913d05197067d6b97df6f1db76d2998af65a1d","created_at":"2026-08-23T03:53:44+00:00","direction":"meta_to_principle","generation_trace":[{"attempts":1,"input_sha256":"3ba6ad382f929a6013cd6bbfd8818dacbb4779f986df0b7d56f911be4e34c8d1","input_tokens":5784,"latency_ms":31186,"model":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Flash","output_sha256":"d76039f56013e2ac0061939433a9c3995861d5a174fe66649bddf1f68e3a16e9","output_tokens":2543,"prompt_sha256":"a0e24249a3438877119c33b7ce1b688152e1189df5765ebd53fae91f7c321069","prompt_template":"meta-grounding-v1","provider":"siliconflow","repair_attempted":false,"schema_valid":true,"transport_attempts":1}],"link_id":"foundation-link:9f40bd91b50a1af1f9cc1dc1","meta_principle_id":"meta:physics:second-law","meta_principle_revision":1,"principle_id":"prn:information-control-complexity:01M0PC0H634EYV8XHZD3B9EEC9","principle_revision":1,"rationale":"The dissipative backward-recovery failure in the new principle is consistent with the second law's arrow of time and macroscopic irreversibility. However, the second law concerns thermodynamic entropy in isolated macroscopic systems, whereas the new principle is a formal statement about deterministic dynamical systems, so the compatibility is partial and needs human review.","relation_type":"consistent_with","review_attestation":{"actor":"principia-owner","basis":"Explicit Submit reviewed changeset confirmation in local Admin","reviewed_at":"2026-08-23T08:08:08+00:00","source_review_status":"unassessed","trace_id":"sync:01M0PTK9G6V6VXNVFWAWBHMSYT"},"review_status":"reviewed","revision":1,"scale_compatibility":"partial","schema_version":"global-foundation-link-v1","status":"active","updated_at":"2026-08-23T03:53:44+00:00","variable_compatibility":"partial"}
